Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1c1e5f1f-8d12-9d45-8d44-996d48657766"],

Cell["\<\
1. Visualise window conditioning: In Lab 7A with BSpline (P = 12), switch \
Envelope Window from None to Hann and notice how singular values at edges \
plummet by ~10^4 (explaining why thin-SVD Q-space ADMM is indispensable).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"453a682b-4ebb-6844-a9da-f1cdba6541ef"],

Cell["\<\
2. Natural zero endpoints without windowing: Test FourierSine vs Hann + \
BSpline for vanishing turn-on and turn-off RF amplitudes.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7077acea-4e4b-0243-acf4-e162fef3100d"],

Cell["\<\
3. Spectral bandwidth narrowing: In Lab 7B, lower Param Target P from 16 down \
to 4 on Fourier or BSpline and compare both F_U and the DFT spectral tail.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f92c33d-1883-5440-b4aa-5ca07f520634"],

Cell["\<\
4. Toggle Hard Limits on/off under Hann + BSpline and confirm Optimizer \
switches smoothly to FISTA while maintaining zero boundary amplitude.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4465c2ee-9d6a-c344-bddf-cc2c7c16e5ab"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3e9a65c1-977a-b549-80f3-c89648ee7ca9"],

Cell["\<\
Reduced waveform parameterisations cut degrees of freedom, smoothly shape \
pulse transients, and suppress spectral sidebands while preserving exact \
adjoint gradients. Combining windows with thin-SVD Q-space reduction keeps \
hard circular disk and slew limits accurate even for highly ill-conditioned \
spline bases.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfdc7e88-3468-424b-abbd-b66e38045002"],

